{
  "raw": {
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41589&lang=en": {
      "title": "Temporary Digital Accessibility Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted Date: Nov 2, 2026 Job category: Student/Temp Department: ADM AVCOIT Administration Schedule: Part-time University of Colorado Denver Department: Digital Accessibility, Office of Information Technology Job Title: Temporary Digital Accessibility Coordinator This is a Temporary position limited to no more than 9-months. This position starts January 11, 2027 and is funded through June 30, 2027 Job Summary: The University of Colorado Denver is seeking an organized, detail-oriented, and collaborative Digital Accessibility Coordinator to provide part-time, temporary support for the university's digital accessibility initiatives. Working under the direction of the Digital Accessibility Lead, this position will assist with implementing and coordinating accessibility efforts across the university to help ensure that digital content, instructional materials, websites, and university technologies are accessible to individuals with disabilities. The Digital Accessibility Coordinator will provide hands-on support for identifying and addressing accessibility issues in digital materials, including the use of Ally within the Canvas Learning Management System to help faculty identify accessibility barriers and improve the accessibility of their course content. The position will also support project coordination, accessibility remediation tracking, documentation, training, communication, and collaboration with faculty, staff, and campus partners. The ideal candidate is a proactive problem-solver who is highly organized, comfortable working with digital technologies, and knowledgeable about digital accessibility practices. The position requires someone who can manage assigned tasks independently while working collaboratively with the Digital Accessibility Lead to advance university accessibility initiatives Duties: Digital Accessibility Implementation and Support Assist the Digital Accessibility Lead with implementing and monitoring activities outlined in the university's digital accessibility plan. Monitor and utilize Ally within Canvas to identify accessibility issues, review reports, track remediation progress, and support faculty in improving course content and access to alternative formats. Conduct routine accessibility reviews of digital documents, Canvas course materials, and other digital content. Perform accessibility improvements to digital materials, including Word documents, PowerPoint presentations, PDFs, and instructional content. Coordinate accessibility remediation efforts with faculty, staff, and campus partners, escalating complex issues to the Digital Accessibility Lead or appropriate university partners. Utilize university-approved artificial intelligence (AI) tools, as appropriate, to support accessibility reviews, content remediation, training development, and workflow efficiency. Review AI-generated outputs for accuracy and accessibility while adhering to university policies on responsible AI use, data privacy, and security. Project Coordination and Administrative Support Provide project coordination and administrative support to the Digital Accessibility Lead. Maintain and update project trackers, accessibility remediation records, and progress reports to support the implementation of university accessibility initiatives. Monitor project timelines, communicate updates, and follow up with campus partners on assigned accessibility-related tasks. Assist with coordinating meetings, preparing materials, documenting action items, and tracking follow-up activities. Organize and maintain accessibility resources, procedures, training materials, and reference documentation. Training, Communication, and Outreach Assist the Digital Accessibility Lead with developing and updating accessibility training materials, presentations, guides, and resources for faculty and staff. Support the coordination and delivery of accessibility workshops, training sessions, and campus outreach activities. Provide routine guidance and assistance to faculty and staff on digital accessibility practices, tools, including the use of Ally to identify and address accessibility issues within Canvas courses. Help communicate accessibility best practices and available resources to university departments. Assist with creating accessible instructional materials and communications that encourage faculty and staff to adopt inclusive digital practices. Collect feedback from training participants and campus partners to identify opportunities for improving resources and support. Collaboration and Continuous Improvement Collaborate with the Digital Accessibility Lead and campus partners, including the Office of Information Technology, Disability Resources & Services, and academic and administrative departments. Assist with collecting and organizing information related to digital accessibility concerns, requests, and remediation efforts to support reporting and continuous improvement. Support ongoing efforts to improve accessibility workflows, resources, and processes. Stay informed about digital accessibility practices, tools, and emerging guidance relevant to the position. Perform other related duties as assigned in support of university digital accessibility initiatives. Work Location: Hybrid – this role follows a hybrid work arrangement and requires the employee to work on campus/in the office as needed to support operational and departmental needs. Why Join Us: The Office of Information Technology (OIT) supports CU Denver’s mission by providing technology and services that advance teaching, learning, research, and university operations. OIT helps students, faculty, and staff access resources, achieve their goals, and work more effectively. As part of OIT, the Digital Accessibility Coordinator will contribute to meaningful, university-wide initiatives that promote equitable access to digital content and technology. This position offers the opportunity to collaborate with campus partners, develop valuable skills in digital accessibility, and make a direct impact on creating a more accessible and inclusive learning and working environment at CU Denver. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Minimum Qualifications (Required): · Bachelor's degree in information technology, instructional design, education, communications, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience, subject to university classification requirements. · Experience supporting digital content management, project coordination, technical assistance, accessibility initiatives, or related work. Familiarity with digital accessibility principles, inclusive digital content practices, or accessibility evaluation tools. Experience working with Microsoft Office applications, digital document management systems, and online collaboration tools. Preferred Qualifications: · Experience supporting digital accessibility initiatives, assessments, or remediation activities. · Experience using Ally or similar accessibility evaluation tools within a learning management system to identify accessibility issues and support improvements to digital course materials. · Familiarity with the Canvas Learning Management System and accessibility best practices for online instructional content. · Experience reviewing and improving the accessibility of digital documents, including Word documents, PowerPoint presentations, and PDFs. · Familiarity with Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 Level A and AA and Colorado accessibility requirements, including HB21-1110. · Familiarity with assistive technologies and accessibility evaluation tools. · Experience working in a higher education setting. · Experience coordinating projects, meetings, training sessions, or cross-departmental initiatives. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities · Knowledge of digital accessibility principles, standards, and best practices. · Familiarity with learning management systems and tools used to evaluate and improve digital accessibility. · Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage multiple priorities. · Ability to perform routine digital accessibility reviews and improvements to digital content. · Ability to interpret accessibility evaluation results and communicate recommendations clearly to faculty and staff. · Strong interpersonal, communication, and customer service skills. · Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and campus partners. · Ability to independently manage assigned tasks while working under the direction of the Digital Accessibility Lead. · Strong problem-solving skills and willingness to seek guidance when addressing complex accessibility issues. · Commitment to accessibility, inclusion, and equitable access to digital information and technology. · Ability to effectively and responsibly use AI-enabled tools to support digital accessibility tasks, improve workflows, and develop accessible content, with appropriate human review and quality assurance. · Demonstrated ability to organize and track multiple projects, manage priorities, and maintain accurate records and documentation. · Strong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively with individuals from different technical and professional backgrounds. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): 1. A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position 2. Curriculum vitae / Resume 3. Five professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers . Questions should be directed to: Kady Katona at kady.katona@ucdenver.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Immediately and continues until November 15 th . Anticipated Pay Range: The hiring range for this position has been established at: $28.00 to $32.00 / hour. The above hiring range represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. Temporary employees are only eligible for sick leave benefits. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: The University of Colorado (CU) is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@ucdenver.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Denver is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41606&lang=en": {
      "title": "CU Denver Prevention, Education, and Outreach Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted Date: Nov 4, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: EVC CAO Administration Schedule: Full-time University of Colorado Anschutz Department: Office of Equity Job Title: CU Denver Prevention, Education, and Outreach Coordinator Position #: 00669095 – Requisition #: 41606 Job Summary: The Office of Equity (OE) is currently seeking a Prevention, Education, and Outreach (PEO) Coordinator to increase the visibility of the OE for CU Denver on the Auraria Campus. The PEO Coordinator will develop materials and trainings on topics related to the CU’s Nondiscrimination and Sexual Misconduct, Intimate Partner Violence, and Stalking Policies, federal and state civil rights laws, including Titel VI, Title VII, Title IX, VAWA, and Clery, and other prevention topics, such as bystander intervention. The PEO Coordinator will be responsible for organizing and facilitating in-person and remote trainings for CU Denver on the Auraria Campus, including the student online compliance training. This position works alongside the CU Anschutz Prevention, Education, and Outreach Coordinator on dual-campus programs, including the website and employee online compliance training. The CU Denver PEO Coordinator will assist the OE with their annual review of University policy and procedures related to federal and state civil rights laws, and conduct additional research and assessments of program effectiveness and campus climate. Supervision Received: This position reports to the Associate Vice Chancellor for Institutional Equity. Supervision Exercised: No current supervision responsibilities, but may supervise interns, graduate, and/or student staff, as requested. Key Responsibilities: Prevention and Education (50%) : Develop and facilitate in-person and remote educational workshops and trainings for students and employees of CU Denver using evidence-informed prevention practices focused on increasing awareness about the university’s nondiscrimination and sexual misconduct policies and increasing knowledge and skills to preventing discrimination, harassment, and sexual misconduct, including but not limited to ethical bystander intervention and consent education. Ensure that trainings and educational materials are compliant with University policies, as well as Titel VI, Title VII, Title IX, VAWA, the Clery Act, and other relevant federal and state laws. Establish and maintain positive working relationships with key stakeholders at CU Denver through the development, planning, and implementation of educational trainings and workshops adapted to their needs and requests. Assist with the development, implementation, and management of the required yearly online CANVAS training for all CU Denver students aimed at increasing awareness and understanding of CU’s Nondiscrimination and Sexual Misconduct, Intimate Partner Violence and Stalking policies, bystander intervention techniques, avenues for reporting, and supportive remedies and resources. Work with the CU system team to assist with the development, implementation, and management of the required online Percipio training for all CU Denver employees aimed at providing education about discrimination, sexual misconduct, reporting, and bystander intervention. Develop and distribute visually appealing marketing, branding, and outreach materials, including those aimed at being shared on social media, the OE website, or within departmental communications. This includes brochures, posters, and other print materials to support ongoing prevention and training efforts. Outreach (20%): Provide ongoing in-person and electronic outreach to CU Denver schools, colleges, and departments to inquire about training opportunities and provide information about the OE, and build positive working relationships. Attend in-person and remote campus meetings and events as a representative of the OE to raise awareness and increase visibility of the OE’s support services for CU Denver constituents. Actively foster and support a university climate that celebrates our differences and supports individual faculty, staff, and student growth and encourages personal development, personal accountability, self-reflection, and academic success. Assessment (20%) : Assess compliance with and effectiveness of the required yearly online CANVAS training for all CU students and provide reports to the OE and campus leadership upon request. Assess the effectiveness of outreach efforts, prevention programs, educational workshops, and trainings. Assess compliance with the required online Percipio training for all CU Denver employees and provide yearly compliance reports to the OE, campus departments, and leadership. Assess the training and educational needs of departments and adapt materials and trainings accordingly. Provide timely assessment and evaluation data to OE staff to be included in the annual report, including but not limited to training attendance, compliance rates, and program effectiveness. Create surveys and other assessments related to campus climate as requested and facilitate the collection of university data. Work with the OE team to ensure that the OE meets its compliance obligations to offer and evaluate training related to Title VII, Title IX, VAWA, the Clery Act, and other relevant state and federal laws. Utilize data to drive prevention, education, and outreach programming that targets areas of need. Other (10%) : Collaborate with the CU Anschutz PEO Coordinator as appropriate. Fill in for the CU Anschutz PEO Coordinator when available and as appropriate. In collaboration with the CU Anschutz PEO Coordinator, update the OE website specific to prevention, education, and outreach. May supervise interns, graduate, and/or student staff, as requested. Perform other duties as assigned. Work Location: Hybrid – this role is eligible for a hybrid schedule on campus and as needed for in-person meetings. This position will be working on the Denver Campus. Why Join Us: The CU Denver | CU Anschutz Office of Equity’s (OE) mission is to foster a university community where all identities are respected and every community member has equitable access to educational and employment opportunities. The OE achieves this through transparent case resolutions, impartial investigations, support and safety measures, and comprehensive prevention education. The OE also oversees compliance with the University of Colorado Nondiscrimination Policy, the Sexual Misconduct, Intimate Partner Violence, and Stalking Policy, and the Consensual Amorous Relationships Policy. Why work for the University? We have AMAZING benefits and offer exceptional amounts of holiday, vacation and sick leave! The University of Colorado offers an excellent benefits package including: Medical: Multiple plan options Dental: Multiple plan options Additional Insurance: Disability, Life, Vision Retirement 401(a) Plan: Employer contributes 10% of your gross pay Paid Time Off: Accruals over the year Vacation Days: 22/year (maximum accrual 352 hours) Sick Days: 15/year (unlimited maximum accrual) Holiday Days: 15/year Tuition Benefit: Employees have access to this benefit on all CU campuses ECO Pass: Reduced rate RTD Bus and light rail service There are many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor’s degree in Public Health, Education, Social Sciences, Social Work, Ethnic Studies, Public Administration, Communications, Sociology, a medical field, or another directly related field from an accredited institution. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/military/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year for year basis. At least 1 year of professional training experience in higher education, human resources, diversity/inclusion, advocacy, civil rights investigations, employee relations, a medical field, or another related field. Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in Social Work, Ethnic Studies, Public Health or Administration, History, Sociology, Higher Education Administration, Adult Learning, Organizational Development, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. At least 2 years of experience in facilitating workshops and developing curriculum specific to diversity, equity, inclusion, and/or the prevention of sexual assault, domestic violence, and stalking. Demonstrated experience with providing high-impact campus-wide culturally engaging educational programs in person and online/virtual formats. Conditions of Employment: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States without requiring sponsorship. We are unable to provide work visa sponsorship or employment authorization for this position now or in the future. This position will be working on both Denver and Anschutz Medical Campus. This position is anticipated to have a flexible hybrid working option that is subject to change at any time based on University requirements. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to sit for long period of time. Tasks may involve looking at computer screen continuously for long periods of time. Must occasionally lift and/or move up to 20 pounds. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Outstanding customer service skills. Exercise judgment and independent initiative; handle sensitive matters that require confidentiality. Highly organized professional with high integrity and discretion; Ability to work expediently, timely, and proficiently, to apply appropriate solutions to identified problems. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to create publicity materials aimed at being posted online and or in print media (i.e., social media posts, website materials, brochures, and posters). Ability to engage learners in a way that fosters active participation in the learning process. Ability to work well across organizational levels and division to accomplish campus and unit goals in collaboration with key constituencies. Ability to work with diverse and multicultural populations. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with professionals at all levels Proficiency with word processing, (i.e., word), presentation (i.e., PowerPoint), tracking (i.e., excel), and scheduling (i.e., Outlook) software. How to Apply: For full consideration, please submit the following document(s): A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position Curriculum vitae / Resume Three to five professional references, including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address Questions should be directed to: Mercy Booth, Mercy.booth@cuanschutz.edu Screening of Applications Begins: Applications will be accepted until finalists are identified, but preference will be given to complete applications received by 11/17/2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Anticipated Pay Range: The starting salary range ( or hiring range ) for this position has been established as $54,656 - $63,614. The above salary range ( or hiring range ) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position may be eligible for overtime compensation, depending on the level. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Total Compensation Calculator Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. ADA Statement: The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at hr.adacoordinator@cuanschutz.edu ​. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado Anschutz is dedicated to ensuring a safe and secure environment for our faculty, staff, students and visitors. To assist in achieving that goal, we conduct background investigations for all prospective employees. Vaccination Statement: CU Anschutz strongly encourages vaccination against the COVID-19 virus and other vaccine preventable diseases . If you work, visit, or volunteer in healthcare facilities or clinics operated by our affiliated hospital or clinical partners or by CU Anschutz, you will be required to comply with the vaccination and medical surveillance policies of the facilities or clinics where you work, visit, or volunteer, respectively. In addition, if you work in certain research areas or perform certain safety sensitive job duties, you must enroll in the occupational health medical surveillance program ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41607&lang=en": {
      "title": "Development Assistant",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/18/2026 Posted Date: Nov 4, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM-CHAN Advancement Denver Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Admin Assistant II Working Title: Development Assistant (Term Limited) FTE: Full-time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid *Term Limited* Salary Range: $50,381 - $55,684 Position #00691710– Requisition #41026 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Office of Advancement connects those who are passionate about education and research to the people and programs at CU Denver who can excel with their support. We serve as a trusted campus and community resource that inspires alumni pride and private support to advance CU Denver's mission, and we work to ensure a bright and promising future for CU Denver through robust engagement, transformative philanthropy, and a deep sense of pride in the university. The Development Assistant will perform administrative duties and tasks, reflecting substantial variety and complexity, in the Office of Advancement. *This is a term limited position that is currently funded through June 30th 2029. The position will be reviewed by January 2029 to assess financial sustainability. If your term of employment will be concluded based on a lack of funding, you will be provided 30 days notice of the termination of the term of employment in writing by the University.* Development Assistant What you will do: Provides general office support including but not limited to catering orders, organization of office and donor events, purchasing donor flowers/gifts, printing support, receipts, reservations, and facilitating guest parking. Performs research and updates, fund and EID look-up support in Salesforce (CU Ascend) for Advancement staff. Serves as a data and records management resource as it relates to Advancement – understanding the data platforms, information stored and appropriate tools to access requested information. Serves as primary point of contact and day to day operations for gift handling, accepting donations, creating accurate records and ensuring timely delivery to the Gift Processing unit at the CU Foundation. Provides backup front desk coverage and presence to greet, direct, and address questions and concerns of visitors in person, as well as via phone and email. Manages general triage for the Advancement and DA Support email accounts, sorting and distributing mail, scheduling conference rooms, and facilitating meeting setup. Acts as liaison between the CU Foundation, CU System, and CU Denver campus partners regarding questions, research information, reports, and operations. Supports team with event bios and briefings for personal meetings, prospect lists, and analyses as needed. Supports certain events as assigned including but not limited to mailing, packaging, event assembly, prep, and take down. Maintains cleanliness and orderliness of communal office space including lobby and kitchen; keeps inventory on office supplies, external communication documents, and swag. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Two (2) years of relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned to this position Substitution: A combination of related education and/or relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned equal to two (2) years Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Experience with data management and/or data research. Experience with Microsoft Excel and CRM database. Professional experience working in non-profit, events, and/or development/fundraising. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Outstanding customer service skills. Proficiency and familiarity with Advance, Salesforce, or similar databases. Proficiency in pulling, extracting, and organizing intricate data reports. Ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing. Ability to utilize internet navigation and research tools (e.g., online, printed, etc.) Proficiency in pulling, extracting, and organizing intricate data reports. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Ability to conceptualize and utilize data. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of access and engagement with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to manage multiple tasks simultaneously, adapt to changing priorities, manage time and meet deadlines. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and internet navigation tools with proven knowledge of word processing, spreadsheet software, email, and internet access software. Conditions of Employment This is a term limited position that is currently funded through June 30th 2029. The position will be reviewed by January 2029 to assess financial sustainability. If your term of employment will be concluded based on a lack of funding, you will be provided 30 days notice of the termination of the term of employment in writing by the University. Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required for Advancement events. This position requires an in-office presence (3 days a week), but does provide flexibility with a hybrid accommodation for remote work at the discretion of the unit. Requires valid driver’s license. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $50,381 - $55,684. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until Nov 18, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: • A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications • A current CV/resume • List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Nickolas Chabot-Olson, Nickolas.Chabot-Olson@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41593&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assessment Office Principal Professional (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/18/2026 Posted Date: Nov 3, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: SEHD DEAN Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Business Services Principal Professional Working Title: Assessment Office Principal Professional (Part-Time) FTE: Part-Time 60% (0.60 FTE) | Hybrid Salary Range: $49,017 - $54,177, prorated for 0.60 (60%) FTE Position #00788069– Requisition #41593 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit cudenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Assessment Office Principal Professional role supports (federal, state, and voluntary) external reporting and any institutional research efforts connected to the SEHD, including but not limited to strategic planning, and assessment and outcome measurement for Continuing Professional Education programs (e.g., ASPIRE to Teach). Assessment Office Principal Professional (Part-Time) What you will do: Accreditation, Authorization, and Other External Reporting Support the preparation for state and accreditation self-studies and site visits with other SEHD leaders (i.e., Associate Deans, Assistant Deans, Directors, Program Leaders). Manage annual and ad hoc federal, state, accreditation, and media-related reporting (i.e., Title II, SURDS, DADC, TEACH Colorado, CACREP, COAMFTE, NASP, APA, APBA, US News,). Develop and maintain a comprehensive portfolio of accreditation requirements, deadlines, and documentation for all SEHD programs; monitoring changes in accreditation standards and regulatory requirements and advising others including leadership on necessary adjustments. Assessment and Outcomes Measurement Support the design and tracking of data related to strategic SEHD efforts, e.g., D2/D3 efforts. Support efforts to demonstrate outcomes and impact of SEHD graduates from Continuing Professional Education programs including ASPIRE to Teach (i.e., mission and vision fulfillment, skills and competencies, impact on P-21 students, knowledge of content and pedagogy, performance as educators and human service professionals, leadership in field, persistence in field). Support the ASPIRE faculty in Coordinating, maintaining, and aggregating program assessment data Data Management and Reporting Develop, implement, and/or manage reporting to support both external (federal, state, accreditation) and internal data needs, using statistical software as needed and various reporting mediums that are suited to the audience (e.g., dashboards, queries, PPT, Word, Excel). Manage response to ad-hoc data requests from SEHD leadership, faculty, and staff. Partner with internal and external colleagues including SEHD IT and CU Denver OIRE teams in the collection, warehousing, and reporting of SEHD data. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. A bachelor’s degree in business, business administration, finance, accounting, education, social sciences, healthcare administration, public administration, communications, information systems, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Three years of relevant experience, including the use of large datasets for reporting purposes Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Master's or terminal degree in business, business administration, finance, accounting, education, social sciences, healthcare administration, public administration, communications, information systems, or a directly related field from an accredited institution. Experiences with program evaluation, accreditation processes and licensure programs Experience with designing data bases and quantitative analyses using large data sets Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of and some experience with federal, state, and/or voluntary reporting in higher education. Knowledge of and some experience in data cleaning, analysis, and reporting with a strong attention to detail. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Demonstrate a commitment to providing outstanding customer service skills. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of access and engagement with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to perform duties independently without guidance and direction from other professionals. Ability to articulate the University's mission and the importance of the strategic plan. Ability to manage ambiguous situations and/or information and translate them into results. Ability to manage multiple projects and tasks simultaneously while maintaining a high attention to detail. Ability to effectively plan and establish program goals and objectives. Conditions of Employment This role is eligible to work remote; presence on campus is expected for a minimum of 1 day/week. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $49,017 - $54,177, prorated for 0.60 (60%) FTE. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is/is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until Nov 17, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications A current CV/resume List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to SEHD HR at sehdhr@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41603&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Sculpture",
      "description": "Closing Date: 02/01/2027 Posted Date: Nov 3, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CAM-Visual Arts Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer of Sculpture FTE: .225 per 3 credit course Salary Range: $5,371.19 per 3 credit course Position #00660552 – Requisition #41603 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * At the College of Arts & Media (CAM), we empower a diverse community of makers, scholars, and innovators to thrive in the rapidly evolving creative industries. Through a dynamic blend of critical inquiry, creative exploration, and real-world engagement, CAM prepares students for lives filled with opportunity, meaning, and purpose. Rooted in community and driven by a spirit of intellectual and artistic freedom, CAM embraces risk-takers, visionaries, and cultural disruptors by providing access to cutting-edge technology, global perspectives, and a nurturing environment where bold ideas flourish. CAM offers top-ranked degrees and programs in Film & Television, Media Forensics, Music & Entertainment, and Visual Arts. Lecturer appointments are at-will and teaching assignments are determined on a semester by semester basis. Teaching assignments may fluctuate and are contingent upon the schedule of courses offered each term. Lecturer of Sculpture What you will do: Teach one or two 3-credit courses In class hours = 5.5 hours per week per course + other outside of class hours for preparation and planning, approximately 7-10 hours per week per course. This position reports to the Visual Arts Department Chair and works closely with the Sculpture and Art Practices areas. Examples of Work Performed: Instructing students to use sculpture as a tool for creative expression Evaluating sculptural projects for conceptual and technical merit Introducing students to diverse processes, media and equipment to advance their creative practice and self-expression skills. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. MFA in Sculpture, Studio Arts, Digital Media or Architecture or relevant course of study 1 year teaching experience Experience developing and enforcing safe studio practices Evolving personal art practice (1-5 years experience as a practicing artist) Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) 2-3 years teaching experience. Multidisciplinary personal art practice. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of wood, metal, and or foundry practices through personal professional work and/or previous teaching experience. Experience working with a range of creative professionals and students. Skills in installation and immersive art, digital fabrication, and/or mold making as shown through personal creative work and/or previous teaching experience. Ability to teach and work with a diverse student body. Expertise in leading critiques of sculptural work. Ability to demonstrate sculptural techniques to students. Knowledge of historical and contemporary fine artists, genres, and styles. Knowledge of contemporary fine art practice in global context that links screen based technology with studio practice. Ability to convey complex artistic theories and concepts to students. Ability to foster professional connections for students. Strong interpersonal and communication skills across multiple teaching modalities. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with colleagues, students, and community partners representing a wide range of perspectives. Ability to work autonomously, taking initiative on tasks, and meeting deadlines. Ability to outwardly contribute to a respectful, positive, and professional workspace. Knowledge of emerging trends and technologies in illustration education and practice. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,371.19 per 3 credit course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. This position is not eligible for benefits. Application Deadline Preference will be given to complete applications received by November 14, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Letter of application specifically addressing the position requirements and outlining qualifications. Current CV or résumé. Link to website that includes a portfolio of 15-20 images of creative work. Questions should be directed to Melissa Furness, melissa.furness@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41293&lang=en": {
      "title": "Senior Compensation Analyst",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/16/2026 Posted Date: Nov 3, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: Employee Services Schedule: Full-time Join Our Team and Make a Difference in Higher Education! At the System Administration office at the University of Colorado, we are dedicated to building a workplace where everyone feels valued, supported, and empowered to thrive. Our office is committed to fostering a culture where employees find community, a sense of belonging, and the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to our mission and purpose. By joining our team, you’ll have a direct impact on shaping the future of higher education. In addition to the Office of the Board of Regents, the University of Colorado’s system administration includes 19 units that provide essential services to CU’s campuses in Aurora, Boulder, Colorado Springs, and Denver, as well as the Office of the President. While not a part of any one campus, we are proud to serve in the centralized office for the University system. Together, we ensure CU continues to deliver outstanding education, groundbreaking research, and valuable service to our communities. We believe in creating an environment where the unique experiences and perspectives of everyone are embraced, enriching the work we do and the strategic outcomes we pursue. If you’re passionate about making a difference, contributing to a dynamic team, and supporting a mission that matters, we encourage you to apply and be part of our journey. Learn more about CU System Administration . Position Summary: Employee Services provides the CU community with excellent services from recruitment to retirement. This office provides technical expertise while administering benefits, professional development, payroll, individual tax management, and strategic HR programs. The functional areas of Employee Services include Payroll, Technologies, Benefits, Retirement, Financial Education, Learning and Development, International Tax and Human Resources. The Senior Compensation Analyst serves in a specialist capacity to assist the University of Colorado’s System Administration HR team in performing complex compensation analysis, job level and classification reviews, support of unique compensation requests, annual pay program cycles and activities, and support of data and tools. This role will provide guidance and consultation to the System HR Team HR Partners, and when requested, to System departments and managers, by advising on best practices to attract, motivate, and retain talent while driving sound and compliant employment decisions. This position reports to the Compensation and Talent Program Manager and is exempt from the State of Colorado Classified Staff system. Where You Will Work: Applicants must be Colorado residents or able to relocate to Colorado within a month of starting employment with University of Colorado System Administration. This role is eligible to work remotely within Colorado, with the expectation of being in the office in Denver, CO, 1-3 days a month. Please note, leadership may adjust in-office work requirements with a minimum of three months' notice before any change can be implemented. Equal Opportunity Statement: CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Duties and Responsibilities: Duties and responsibilities of the position include, but are not limited to: Annual Compensation Cycles & Compensation Project Management Collects and provides analysis for activities associated with major annual compensation cycles and projects, in consultation with the Manager and Program Director including: Annual Pay Range Updates: Coordinates, prepares, and validates data and identifies market. movement and trends, and works to support recommendations for annual pay range updates. Annual Compensation Increases (merit): Coordinates and supports the annual compensation increase process, including preparation of data and workbooks, tracking department actions, supporting HR Partners through the process. Talent Reviews: Support department talent review cycles ensuring consistent application of compensation practices. Promotions and Pay Growth: Collects and provides analysis of promotions and pay growth actions. Identifies process gaps, risks, inconsistencies, and opportunities for improvement throughout annual compensation cycles and brings recommendations forward to Compensation leadership. Supports the development and continuous improvement of compensation programs, processes, tools, and resources, including integrating AI tools. Supports complex projects and initiatives and develops or implements new practices, processes, tools, and resources within assigned areas of expertise. Compensation Analysis and Business Partnership Consult with and provide guidance to HR Partners regarding compensation knowledge, data, tools, and resources needed to make informed, consistent, and compliant compensation decisions including: Workforce planning (new positions, backfills, drafting job descriptions) Review of internal equity and compliance Succession Emerging capabilities (AI and other skills) Processing and routing approvals Partners with other HR Specialists team to develop, administer, and continuously improve training, communications, and resources that increase understanding of compensation programs and processes. Oversee tool to track all position reviews and transactions. Manage positions in HRIS system and manage JD Library. Conduct assessments on Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA) and Colorado State System exemption status. Providing analysis and solutions for unique business problems including one-time pay bonuses, pay programs, temporary pay differentials, counter offers, and retention programs. Responsible for regular data and reporting to System HR team, HR Partners, and on an as-needed basis for departments and leadership. Ensure compensation practices meet compliance with particular focus on the Colorado Equal Pay for Equal Work Act. What We Offer: Salary: The anticipated hiring range has been established at $80,000 - $82,000 . CU System Administration takes into consideration a combination of the selected candidate’s education, training and experience as it relates to the position, as well as the position’s scope and complexity, internal pay equity and external market value when determining a salary level for potential new employees. Benefits: With our unparalleled range of benefits, including top-notch healthcare, comprehensive wellness programs, enriching professional development, and a dynamic work-life balance, we ensure your holistic growth and happiness. No-cost or low-cost medical & dental plan options, some inclusive of IVF assistance. Disability, Life, Vision Insurance options. Multiple retirement planning options including a mandatory 401(a) plan where CU contributes 10% of your gross pay, a 401k or 403b plan and a 457 deferred compensation plan. Pre-tax savings plans, such as Health care and Dependent care flexible spending accounts. Embrace a healthy work-life balance with ample sick and vacation leave, along with at least 12 paid holidays. This includes a dedicated week off for winter break. 6 weeks of parental leave to adjust to the joys of parenthood. A tuition benefit program for you and/or your dependents. Free RTD EcoPass and free onsite parking at our 1800 Grant Street Office. Many additional perks & programs with the CU Advantage . Additional taxable fringe benefits may be available. For more information on benefits programs, please review our Comprehensive Benefits Guide . Access our Total Compensation Calculator to see what your total rewards could be at CU. (This position is a University Staff position) Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Please include all relevant experience in your resume to be accurately assessed against these qualifications. You must meet all minimum requirements at the time of application to be considered for this role. Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution of higher education, or equivalent professional experience (professional experience may be substituted for the educational requirement on a year-for-year basis) Three (3) years of experience serving in a human resources capacity including multiple of the following: Experience working in or directly with an HR Compensation function Experience reviewing job descriptions and making determinations on position levels and pay Experience creating, updating, or administering pay ranges Preferred Qualifications: Five (5) years’ equivalent human resources experience, as indicated above, including: At least three (3) of those years working in a dedicated Compensation role Familiarity with human resources systems and procedures (Peoplesoft HCM, Taleo Enterprise Edition, or similar platforms) Experience working with or for an institution of higher education Experience using AI in a business setting Certified Compensation Professional (CCP) Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: To be successful in this position a candidate will need the following: General knowledge and understanding of business/organizational structures Customer service skills, including the ability to actively listen, address customer needs, defuse tense situations, and maintain an open, flexible, and friendly demeanor Oral, written, and listening communication skills, including the ability to accurately interpret what others are saying and convey messages, information, concepts, and details accurately and clearly Computer skills, including the ability to use Microsoft Office programs (i.e. Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, etc.) and learn and experiment with new software and systems Comfort working with databases, website and electronic resources Ability to connect managers and teams to resources and guide them on process Collaboration skills, including the ability to work with others from different areas and backgrounds to reach a common goal Ability to influence managers and department leaders in support of strong decisions Organizational skills, including the ability to set and meet goals, coordinate and facilitate meetings, and make decisions Deep excel knowledge and analytical skills Ability to compile and report on large data sets Ability to prompt artificial intelligence via a large language model (LLM) Knowledge of Colorado Labor and Pay Transparency laws Knowledge of federal labor and FLSA laws and statutes How to Apply: For full consideration, please attach the following as separate documents to your application: A cover letter identifying the job specific minimum qualifications you possess and interest in the position. A resume including all relevant experience to be accurately assessed against the qualifications listed in the posting. Please ensure you check the “Job Specific Attachments” box next to each document on the “Required Documents” page of the application for the appropriate documents to be attached. Per the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, you are not required to provide your date of birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation on your resume or cover letter. If an application requires additional materials, such as a transcript or certification, you may redact identifying information relating to your date or birth, dates of school attendance, or dates of graduation. When to Apply: For full consideration completed applications must be submitted by Monday, November 16, 2026 . Reference checking is a standard step in our hiring process. You may be asked to provide contact information, including email addresses and phone numbers, for up to five references as part of the search process for this position. *Please note: All application materials must be submitted through CU Careers; emailed materials will not be considered. * Sponsorship Statement: We are unable to sponsor applicants for work visas for this position. Background Check Statement: The University of Colorado is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The Immigration Reform and Control Act requires that a verification of employment eligibility be documented for all new employees by the end of the third day of work. The University of Colorado is committed to diversity and equality in education and employment. ADA Statement: We are committed to an inclusive and barrier-free search process. We provide accommodations for applicants requesting accommodation through the search process such as alternative formats of this posting. Individuals with disabilities in need of accommodations throughout the search process should contact the ADA Coordinator at: systemhr@cu.edu ."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41576&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/03/2026 Posted Date: Nov 2, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CLAS-GEOGRAPHY/ENVIRNMENTL SCI Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer FTE: Part-time Salary Range: 5,113-5,546 for a three-credit course. Position #00629022 - Requisition #41576 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver The University of Colorado Denver is the state’s premier public urban research university and equity-serving institution. Globally connected and locally invested, CU Denver partners with future-focused learners and communities to design accessible, relevant, transformative educational experiences for every stage of life and career. Across seven schools and colleges in the heart of downtown Denver, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges through break through innovations and impactful research, and creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. For more information, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description This posting will establish and maintain a pool of part-time lecturers with experience teaching Geography and Environmental Science courses for the Department of Geography & Environmental Sciences in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences at the University of Colorado Denver. By submitting your application, you will become part of an applicant pool. Candidates hired from this pool will fill temporary, non-tenure track positions and will teach no more than two courses (6 credits) per semester. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50%) and will be made semester-by-semester, depending on the needs of the department and subject to budgetary approval. Therefore, this posting does not necessarily reflect a current open position. The Department of Geography & Environmental Sciences will contact you if there is an opening that suits your qualifications. Lecturer What you will do: Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in GEOG, ENVS and/or GEOL, depending on level of qualification. Courses to be taught will be assigned by the department. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Masters degree in Geography, Environmental Science, or a related field from an accredited university Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Previous teaching experience. PhD in Geography, Environmental Science, or related field. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge: Content knowledge in Geography and Environmental Sciences Skills: Excellent Communication and Pedagogical Skills Ability: Teaching Talents: Passion for and experience teaching at the college level in the specified content areas Conditions of Employment This position allows for an onsite presence on campus as well as a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Attend lecturer meetings twice a year (once each semester) to provide feedback to department chair on courses/students, and discuss concerns if any. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements The ability to sit and/or stand for class periods, stand and walk to get to classrooms on campus, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The hiring range for this position has been established at $1,704 per credit hour (lower division), $1,849 per credit hour (upper division and graduate level). The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits statement to include in all benefits-eligible positions. See Eligibility Matrix. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Dec 1, 2026. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A letter of interest describing relevant job experiences as they relate to listed job qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). 2-3 professional references including name, address, phone number (mobile number if appropriate), and email address. (We will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to Angela Carrington, Angela.Carrington@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41562&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Performance (Drum Kit)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/28/2027 Posted Date: Oct 30, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CAM-Music & Entertainment Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer of Performance (Drum Kit) FTE: .33 per half hour student, .66 per hour student Salary Range: $520.20 per half hour student, $1040.40 per hour student Position #00674803 – Requisition #41562 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * At the College of Arts & Media (CAM), we empower a diverse community of makers, scholars, and innovators to thrive in the rapidly evolving creative industries. Through a dynamic blend of critical inquiry, creative exploration, and real-world engagement, CAM prepares students for lives filled with opportunity, meaning, and purpose. Rooted in community and driven by a spirit of intellectual and artistic freedom, CAM embraces risk-takers, visionaries, and cultural disruptors by providing access to cutting-edge technology, global perspectives, and a nurturing environment where bold ideas flourish. CAM offers top-ranked degrees and programs in Film & Television, Media Forensics, Music & Entertainment, and Visual Arts. The Music & Entertainment Industry Studies (MEIS) Department features some of the best contemporary-focused music industry programs in the country. With about 500 students, MEIS has one of the biggest music business, recording arts, singer/songwriter, and contemporary performance programs in the Western U.S. Our downtown Denver location is perfect for enabling our students to be very involved with the thriving Denver music scene while they are in the program. As one of the only music departments in the country with a contemporary focus, Music & Entertainment Industry Studies (MEIS) at CU Denver provides students with the guidance, knowledge, and expertise needed to transform passion for music into a lifelong profession. Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date (DATE) Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three month window if all openings are filled. Lecturer appointments are at-will and teaching assignments are determined on a semester by semester basis. Teaching assignments may fluctuate and are contingent upon the schedule of courses offered each term. Lecturer of Performance (Drum Kit) What you will do: 100% Teaching (Maximum 6 credit hours): As a Lecturer of Performance (Drum Kit), your primary focus will be on inspiring and training the next generation of contemporary drum kit players. This can include instruction in the following: Lower division half hour drum kit lessons Upper division full hour drum kit lessons Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. BA/BS/BM in Music or related field Or tested experience as exemplified by one or more of the following: Recording with a reputable label (corresponding review from a reputable media outlet). Extensive experience as a performer/composer/arranger. Representation with a reputable artist management company which contains an active roster of high level artists. Evidence of a national/international tour/festival. Evidence of song published/performed by a major artist/publishing/media outlet (i.e. film or TV show) or company. Two years of successful experience teaching at a major university or college in same or similar program. High level drum kit performance experience. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Master’s Degree in Music or related field. Experience teaching music at the college level. Experience teaching and performing multiple genre styles or style at a high level. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Proven experience in establishing effective working relationships with a diverse population at all levels throughout the institution—and in the community. Ability to communicate in a positive and effective manner, across various modalities. Ability to balance multiple projects and tasks while maintaining attention to detail. Ability to create equitable and positive experiences for all. Outwardly contribute to a respectful, positive, and professional workspace. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of access and engagement with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to establish work priorities, follow through, and meet established deadlines. Strong judgment and critical thinking skills. Ability to authentically listen and communicate relevant information, anticipate problems, and offer suggestions for resolution. Demonstrated dedication to developing professional relationships with students and alumni. Demonstrate dedication to mentoring students to best realize their potential as artists in society. Commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusivity equitable practices, and inclusive pedagogy Demonstrated excellence and experience in organizational teamwork, communication, and interpersonal skills. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $520.20 per half hour student, $1040.40 per hour student The salary of the finalist(s) s.elected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. This position is not eligible for benefits. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date (Oct 30, 2026). Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three - month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Letter of application specifically addressing the position requirements and outlining qualifications Current CV or résumé Questions should be directed to Evan Shelton, evan.shelton@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41563&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Performance (Electronic Music Performance/Production)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/29/2027 Posted Date: Oct 30, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CAM-Music & Entertainment Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer of Performance (Electronic Music Performance/Production) FTE: .33 per half hour student, .66 per hour student, 1.33 for ensemble Salary Range: $520.20 per half hour student, $1040.40 per hour student, $2,742.96 for ensemble Position #653654 – Requisition #41563 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * At the College of Arts & Media (CAM), we empower a diverse community of makers, scholars, and innovators to thrive in the rapidly evolving creative industries. Through a dynamic blend of critical inquiry, creative exploration, and real-world engagement, CAM prepares students for lives filled with opportunity, meaning, and purpose. Rooted in community and driven by a spirit of intellectual and artistic freedom, CAM embraces risk-takers, visionaries, and cultural disruptors by providing access to cutting-edge technology, global perspectives, and a nurturing environment where bold ideas flourish. CAM offers top-ranked degrees and programs in Film & Television, Media Forensics, Music & Entertainment, and Visual Arts. The Music & Entertainment Industry Studies (MEIS) Department features some of the best contemporary-focused music industry programs in the country. With about 500 students, MEIS has one of the biggest music business, recording arts, singer/songwriter, and contemporary performance programs in the Western U.S. Our downtown Denver location is perfect for enabling our students to be very involved with the thriving Denver music scene while they are in the program. As one of the only music departments in the country with a contemporary focus, Music & Entertainment Industry Studies (MEIS) at CU Denver provides students with the guidance, knowledge, and expertise needed to transform passion for music into a lifelong profession. Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to six (6) months from the posting date [TAC, please include date posted]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six‑month window if all openings are filled. Lecturer appointments are at-will and teaching assignments are determined on a semester by semester basis. Teaching assignments may fluctuate and are contingent upon the schedule of courses offered each term. Lecturer of Performance (Electronic Music Performance/Production) What you will do: 100% Teaching (Maximum 6 credit hours) As a Lecturer of Performance (Electronic Music Performance/Production), your primary focus will be on inspiring and training the next generation of contemporary Electronic Music Producers. This can include instruction in the following: Lower Division Electronic Music Performance Lessons Upper Division Electronic Music Performance Lessons Electronic Music Producers Ensemble Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. BA/BS/BM in Music or related field Or tested experience as exemplified by one or more of the following: Recording with a reputable label which contains an active roster of high level artists (corresponding review from a reputable media outlet) Extensive experience as a performer/composer/arranger Representation with a reputable artist management company Evidence of a national/international tour/festival Evidence of song published/performed by a major artist/publishing/media outlet (i.e. film or TV show) or company Two years of successful experience teaching at a major university or college in same or similar program Extensive electronic music performance experience, including active live performances at local, regional, and/or national venues. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Master’s Degree in Music Experience teaching Music at the college level Experience teaching and performing multiple genre styles or style at a high level Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Proven experience in establishing effective working relationships with a diverse population at all levels throughout the institution—and in the community. Ability to communicate in a positive and effective manner, across various modalities. Ability to balance multiple projects and tasks while maintaining attention to detail. Ability to create equitable and positive experiences for all. Outwardly contribute to a respectful, positive, and professional workspace. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of access and engagement with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to establish work priorities, follow through, and meet established deadlines. Strong judgment and critical thinking skills. Ability to authentically listen and communicate relevant information, anticipate problems, and offer suggestions for resolution. Demonstrated dedication to developing professional relationships with students and alumni. Demonstrate dedication to mentoring students to best realize their potential as artists in society. Commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusivity equitable practices, and inclusive pedagogy. Demonstrated excellence and experience in organizational teamwork, communication, and interpersonal skills. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $520.20 per half hour student, $1040.40 per hour student. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. This position is not eligible for benefits. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 30, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Letter of application specifically addressing the position requirements and outlining qualifications. Current CV or resume. Questions should be directed to Evan Shelton, evan.shelton@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41560&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Music Business (Music Law)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/28/2027 Posted Date: Oct 30, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: CAM-Music & Entertainment Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer of Music Business (Music Law) FTE: .225 per 3 credit course Salary Range : $5,371.19 per 3 credit course Position #00651317 – Requisition #41560 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado - Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $800 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * At the College of Arts & Media (CAM), we empower a diverse community of makers, scholars, and innovators to thrive in the rapidly evolving creative industries. Through a dynamic blend of critical inquiry, creative exploration, and real-world engagement, CAM prepares students for lives filled with opportunity, meaning, and purpose. Rooted in community and driven by a spirit of intellectual and artistic freedom, CAM embraces risk-takers, visionaries, and cultural disruptors by providing access to cutting-edge technology, global perspectives, and a nurturing environment where bold ideas flourish. CAM offers top-ranked degrees and programs in Film & Television, Media Forensics, Music & Entertainment, and Visual Arts. The Music & Entertainment Industry Studies (MEIS) Department features some of the best contemporary-focused music industry programs in the country. With about 500 students, MEIS has one of the biggest music business, recording arts, singer/songwriter, and contemporary performance programs in the Western U.S. Our downtown Denver location is perfect for enabling our students to be very involved with the thriving Denver music scene while they are in the program. As one of the only music departments in the country with a contemporary focus, Music & Entertainment Industry Studies (MEIS) at CU Denver provides students with the guidance, knowledge, and expertise needed to transform passion for music into a lifelong profession. Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to six (6) months from the posting date of (TAC, please include date of posting here). Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the six month window if all openings are filled. Lecturer appointments are at-will and teaching assignments are determined on a semester by semester basis. Teaching assignments may fluctuate and are contingent upon the schedule of courses offered each term. Lecturer of Music Business (Music Law) What you will do: 100% Teaching You will teach one or two classes per semester (3 - 6 credit hours) As a Lecturer in Music Business (Music Law), your primary focus will be on inspiring and training the next generation of contemporary musicians. This can include instruction in the following: Music Law Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. BA/BS/BM in Music or related field OR; a substitution of tested experience as exemplified by one or more of the following: Experience working in a law specific area of the Music Industry. Experience working for a reputable record label or live production company. Experience managing a reputable music artist. Experience in marketing artists and/or music events. Experience in music publishing. Experience in working with or for a digital music service provider. Two years successful experience teaching at a major university or college in same or similar program. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Master’s Degree in Music or related field. Experience teaching music at a college level. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate in a positive and effective manner, across various modalities. Ability to balance multiple projects and tasks while maintaining attention to detail. Ability to create equitable and positive experiences for all. Outwardly contribute to a respectful, positive, and professional workspace. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of access and engagement with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to establish work priorities, follow through, and meet established deadlines. Strong judgment and critical thinking skills. Ability to authentically listen and communicate relevant information, anticipate problems, and offer suggestions for resolution. Demonstrate dedication to mentoring students to best realize their potential as artists in society. Demonstrated excellence and experience in organizational teamwork, communication, and interpersonal skills. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,371.19 per 3 credit course. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation.This position is not eligible for benefits. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date of (Oct 30, 2026). Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three-month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Letter of application specifically addressing the position requirements and outlining qualifications. Current CV or résumé. Questions should be directed to Evan Shelton, evan.shelton@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41375&lang=en": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/30/2026 Posted Date: Oct 30, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: ADM-CHAN Advancement Denver Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Executive Assistant Working Title: Executive Assistant FTE: Full-time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range : $72,000 - $78,000 Position #00001288 – Requisition #41375 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . The University of Colorado Denver is a leading public urban research university located in the heart of downtown Denver, where academic excellence, innovation and community partnership come together to expand opportunity and strengthen communities. Within this dynamic institution, the School of Education & Human Development is a statewide and national leader in educational quality, access and equity across the lifespan, from birth through higher education. SEHD prepares equity-minded educators, counselors, researchers and leaders who create meaningful change in schools, families and communities across Colorado and beyond. Through innovative academic programs, impactful research and deep community partnerships, the school advances well-being, opportunity and lifelong learning in diverse urban, rural and global communities. The Director of Development will join SEHD at an important moment of opportunity, building philanthropic partnerships that expand student access, elevate faculty and research, and extend the school’s impact for generations to come. Executive Assistant What you will do: Provide administrative and technical support to the Vice Chancellor for Advancement under the direction of the Strategic Advisor. Coordinate day-to-day activities of the Office of Advancement, handling a broad range of inquiries and assignments. The position possesses project management skills, effective analytical and problem-solving skills, works well under pressure, and can handle complex and concurrent tasks. The position exercises initiative to achieve goals and objectives, maintains confidentiality and establishes and maintains positive working relationships. Key Responsibilities: Provide executive support to the Vice Chancellor of Advancement and members of the Advancement leadership group. Manage Office of Advancement administrative activities/projects. Curates and prioritizes lists of key stakeholders for Chancellor engagement, guiding these lists through multiple layers of internal approval processes to ensure value adds for the Chancellor and campus, and collaborating weekly with the Chancellor’s support staff to schedule and facilitate strategic donor interactions and initiatives. From start to finish, ensure seamless execution of tracking follow-through on action items, preparing detailed briefings and talking points for each interaction, and advising on the structure and content of events and meetings to maximize engagement and alignment with Advancement, Chancellor, and institutional goals. Conduct background & preparation research and compile information for upcoming meetings that include the Vice Chancellor and/or members of the Advancement leadership group. Track and follow up on action items from leadership meetings led by the Vice Chancellor for Advancement and/or by the Strategic Advisor Manage special projects of strategic importance to the Office of Advancement. Manage the Vice Chancellor’s and members of the Advancement leadership group’s calendars, ensuring that engagements are appropriately and sensitively prioritized and managed. Respond in a timely manner to all requests from various sources, both internal and external, for the Vice Chancellor’s time. Coordinate meetings and events that include Vice Chancellor and/or members of the Advancement leadership group. Coordinate departmental agendas, support agenda planning, take notes, and track follow up for meetings that include Vice Chancellor for Advancement. Assist with managing expenses, preparing expense reports, reconciliation, and mileage/travel reports for Vice Chancellor for Advancement under the direction of the Executive Director of Finance & Administration. Provides back-up office presence when needed. Performs all other duties as assigned. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Bachelor’s degree in business, public administration, communications, marketing, social science, or a related field from an accredited institution. 4+ years administrative support experience. Substitution: A combination of education and related technical/paraprofessional experience may be substituted for the bachelor’s degree on a year-for-year basis. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) At least three (3) years of experience working in a complex university environment with progressive responsibility. Experience with program or project management with ability to effectively lead a team to accomplish critical strategic objectives. Experience with Concur, or similar procurement and travel software, CRM database, & Microsoft Suite. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of, or desire to learn, university policies and procedures, and ability to apply them Strong attention to detail and organizational skills Demonstrate commitment to providing a high level of responsive, thoughtful, and solutions-oriented service to university leadership, colleagues, donors, volunteers, and external partners. Strong communication skills and the ability to work well with a wide audience. Exceptional attention to detail and demonstrate ability to consistently produce accurate, complete work while managing multiple concurrent priorities. Proficiency with communication, word processing, spreadsheet, presentation, and scheduling software (such as Microsoft Outlook, Teams, Word, Excel, Access, PowerPoint, and Adobe Professional). Ability to take dictation. Ability to manage executive email inboxes. Ability to exercise sound judgment, independently prioritize competing and time-sensitive requests, and recognize when an issue requires escalation. Ability to communicate proactively, particularly when priorities change, deadlines may be affected, information is missing or additional clarification is needed. Ability to interact and partner positively with students, faculty, staff, administrators, donors, and visitors. Ability to establish work priorities and adapt to changing needs. Ability to follow through to ensure completion of activities by the deadline established. Ability to communicate effectively with all levels of faculty, administration, staff and students in both a written and verbal capacity. Ability to manage complex, sensitive, and confidential information. Ability to cooperate and support other department staff in order to contribute to a productive work environment. Ability to develop office processes as needed. Ability to work both individually and as a team with the support staff for the Chancellors and other Associate/Vice Chancellors. Other Variables This position will be expected to be in the office four days out of the week. This individual will be provided a remote work day of their choosing. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $72,000-$78,000. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Oct 26, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications. A current CV/resume. List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references). Questions should be directed to nickolas.chabot-olson@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41539&lang=en": {
      "title": "Graduate Academic Records and Administration Coordinator",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/25/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: VCASA/EVCASA Academic&Stdnt Af Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Academic Services Senior Professional Working Title: Graduate Academic Records and Administration Coordinator FTE: Full-time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid | Term – Limited Salary Range: $63,000 - $65,846 Position #00853744– Requisition #41539 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * *This is a term limited position that is currently funded for 1.5 Years (18 Months).* The position will be reviewed after 18 months of employment to assess financial sustainability. If your term of employment will be concluded based on a lack of funding, you will be provided 30 days’ notice of the term of employment in writing by the University. About GSO The newly reconstituted Graduate Studies Office (GSO) supports graduate students, faculty, and programs at CU Denver by defining and maintaining campus wide graduate policies and procedures; coordinating administration of graduate assistantships and tuition remission; overseeing academic progress and degree completion; and advancing enrollment, retention, and student engagement initiatives. The Graduate Academic Records and Administration Coordinator is a faculty- and staff-focused position that provides leadership and support for all academic administration activities of the Graduate Studies Office at the University of Colorado Denver. Job functions include tasks like coordinating with graduate program directors, graduate council, registrar, and admissions to develop and maintain transparent and campus-consistent catalog access to campus-consistent policies and procedures for all graduate certificates, licensures, and degrees; coordinating with academic affairs, HR, and faculty affairs to ensure faculty and program compliance with campus-level accreditation expectations; coordination with program directors, registrar, and admissions to provide comprehensive and consistent process for documents and records related to student admissions and progress; coordinating student training in pedagogy; coordinating faculty training in student mentoring; other activities that directly support the academic mission of the Graduate Studies Office. Supervision of student employees may be required. Graduate Academic Records and Administration Coordinator What you will do: Graduate Program Information and Accreditation Compliance Partner with academic affairs to ensure campus (HLC) accreditation compliance for all certificates, licenses, and (D1, D2, D3) degree programs. Partner with program directors, admissions, and registrar to scaffold catalog templates for communicating certificate and program information in the graduate academic catalog. Maintain GSO website to provide transparent, comprehensive and consistent access to admissions and graduation requirements for all (D1, D2, D3) degree programs. Graduate Student Academic Records Partner with program directors, registrar, and admissions to improve campus-consistent systems for routing academic forms that are maintained in the student applications and record management systems Manage emails related to graduate student records and appeals submitted to the graduateeducation@ucdenver.edu inbox Graduate Faculty Appointment Records Partner with graduate council, faculty affairs, HR, institutional research and effectiveness to develop and maintain updates and campus-wide access to the annotated list of graduate faculty members. Manage website, documents, and schedule for graduate council. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university, or 4 years of relevant experience in an occupation related to the work assigned to this position. Two (2) years of experience in higher education administrative support. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Four (4) years of experience in higher education administrative support. Master’s or terminal degree from an accredited college or university. Experience with university website, catalog, admissions, and student records software. Familiarity with accreditation requirements for graduate programs. Familiarity with diversity of graduate program types. Experience coordinating cross-disciplinary teams in higher education settings. Prior experience working in the Graduate Studies Office or Graduate School at CU Denver. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to communicate effectively. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels across the university. Ability to perform duties independently without guidance and direction from other professionals. Ability to manage multiple projects and tasks that require high attention to detail. Ability to manage day-to-day workflow, administration, and oversight of project processes. Conditions of Employment This is a term-limited position that is currently funded for 18 months Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $63,000 – 65,846. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training.The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Nov 10, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications A current CV/resume List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Mike Wunder, michael.wunder@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41542&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Marketing",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/25/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Marketing FTE: Part-time, Less than 50% (0.50) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per 3-credit graduate course Position #00853110– Requisition #41542 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Business School at the University of Colorado Denver (CU Denver) seeks to establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers in Marketing from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. Lecturer in Marketing What you will do: Lecturers selected from this pool will teach Marketing classes in the Business School at the University of Colorado Denver. Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Lecturers teaching these classes will instruct in either one or multiple teaching modalities (in-person, online-remote, or hybrid). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in Marketing or other related degrees. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least eight years of duties and responsibilities. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Prior experience teaching in closely related course topic. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in related discipline. Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of diversity, equity, and inclusion with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). A cover letter which specifically addresses job requirements and outlines qualifications List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41534&lang=en": {
      "title": "Executive Director for Student Transitions and Family Engagement",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/18/2026 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: University Staff Department: Student Success & Transitions Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Official Title: Executive Director Working Title: Executive Director for Student Transitions and Family Engagement FTE : Full-time 1.0 (100%) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: 105,000 – 115,000 Position #00679912– Requisition #41534 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Executive Director for Student Transitions and Family Engagement (STFE) provides leadership, direction, and long-term planning for programs that support students through key transitions and foster early engagement in the university experience. The portfolio includes New Student Orientation and Family Engagement, First-Year Experiences, and Peer Advocate Leaders. The Executive Director collaborates with colleagues and student leaders in STFE to ensure alignment with unit, divisional, and institutional priorities that support a coordinated, student-centered approach to student success. This role also serves as a key collaborator within the Division of Strategic Enrollment and Student Success (SESS), continually evaluating and implementing innovative approaches to support student success across in-person, hybrid, and remote environments. Executive Director for Student Transitions and Family Engagement: What you will do: Provide leadership and development for professional staff and student employees, including onboarding, performance management and evaluation, training, team building, and workplace wellness. Provide oversight and strategic management to the following programs: New Student Orientation and Family Engagement, including orientation experiences for first-year and transfer students and their families, extended orientation, enrollment efforts, and innovative onboarding and reengagement initiatives. First-Year Experience programs, including course offerings through First-Year Seminar and College Success (UNIV 1110), and faculty recruitment, training, and development. Peer Advocate Leader (PAL) program, including innovative peer mentoring for new undergraduates, and opportunities for student development. Lynx Summer Academy (i.e., summer bridge) for first-year students, including program planning, recruitment, course selection, program evaluation, and funding acquisition. Foster cross-campus collaboration and partnerships with academic departments, student support offices, faculty, staff, and other university stakeholders to coordinate services, identify emerging student needs, and develop integrated approaches to student engagement, persistence, and success. Establish and advance continuous improvement efforts across assigned programs and services, using best practices, student feedback, and relevant data to evaluate effectiveness, strengthen student outcomes, and align initiatives with university and Student Success goals. Provide reports to leadership on orientation and registration of new students, FYE persistence and retention, and Lynx Summer Academy persistence and retention. Streamline and continually improve communications with students and families by coordinating with Admissions and University Communications to ensure that all outreach to students are timely, specific, and targeted. Oversight of all program budgets and work with Directors to ensure resources allocated for each fiscal year are effectively deployed and processed in alignment with institutional procedures and policies. Participate in committee work with SESS and academic affairs colleagues to improve access, streamlined transitions, and student success and development. Represent CU Denver and STFE at events and programs on and off-campus. Serve on campus committees, working groups, and/or task forces related to Student Success initiatives. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s degree from an accredited institution in related field. Seven (7) years of progressively responsible leadership experience in a higher education setting leading student enrollment, retention, graduation efforts, and/or other related higher education experience. Five (5) years of experience in a supervisory or administrative position in higher education or similar field (i.e., education, business or non-profit). Experience managing budgets. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Earned doctorate in educational leadership or higher education or related field from an accredited institution. Experience in a comprehensive urban university. Experience with traditional age, older, and diverse student populations. Evidence of effective creation and execution of programs that are best-practice informed models. Experience with grant administration, pre- and/or post-award. Experience working with EAB Navigate360. Demonstrated experience leading a team of diverse faculty, staff, and community members. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated ability to lead a team of diverse faculty, staff, and community members. Demonstrated evidence of the ability to effectively devise and manage budgets. Demonstrated commitment to academic excellence and student success. Leadership experience and skills in conceiving and carrying forward new initiatives. Skills in identifying problems, analyzing data, and making recommendations. Ability to be creative, innovative, and willing to take risks to accomplish the goals of the institution. Strong interpersonal skills. Consensus builder with the ability to bring about constructive change using participatory processes. Excellent organizational and coordinating skills. Skilled in communicating effectively in writing, public presentations, and individual or group consultations. A demonstrated ability to integrate principles of equity and inclusion into programs and practices. Ability to work in partnership with faculty, administrators, staff, and students from across the university. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Ability to successfully prioritize among multiple tasks and manage multiple project on distinct timelines. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position generally requires an onsite presence on campus; however, employees may be allowed to work remotely up to one day per week. The ability to work remotely will be determined by the supervisor. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $105,000 – $115,000. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Your total compensation goes beyond the number on your paycheck. The University of Colorado Denver provides generous leave, health plans and retirement contributions that add to your bottom line. Benefits: https://www.cu.edu/employee-services/benefits Total Compensation Calculator: http://www.cu.edu/node/153125 Application Deadline Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Preference will be given to complete applications received by Nov 17, 2026, 11:59:00 PM. Those who do not apply by this date may or may not be considered. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses the job requirements and outlines qualifications A current CV/resume List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Erika Larson, erika.larson@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41508&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Management",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/26/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Management FTE: Part-time, less than 50% (0.50) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range : $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per 3-credit graduate course Position #00715302 – Requisition #41508 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Denver Business School seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. The CU Denver Business School Management program seeks to establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions for the 2026-2027 academic year will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. Lecturer in Management What you will do: Lecturers selected from this pool will teach Management classes in the CU Denver Business School. Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Lecturers teaching these classes will instruct in either one or multiple teaching modalities (in-person, online-remote, or hybrid). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in Management or closely related field. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least five years of related experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in related discipline. Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of diversity, equity, and inclusion with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. Depending on course modality, this position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials : To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Please note that upon hire, applicants will be asked to provide original transcript(s) of their highest degree and two (2) letters of recommendation. Questions should be directed to Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41507&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in International Business",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/26/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in International Business FTE: Part-time, less than 50% (0.50) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range : $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per 3-credit graduate course Position # 00756279 – Requisition #41507 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Denver Business School is seeking applications for a Lecturer in International Business position. This posting will establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions for the 2026-2027 academic year will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. Lecturer in International Business What you will do: The Lecturer(s) selected will teach in the International Business discipline at the CU Denver Business School. Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Classes will be facilitated in varying modalities (in person, hybrid, remote or online). Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in International Business, MBA, International Studies, or closely related field. a closely related field to the course topic. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least five years of duties and responsibilities. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Prior experience teaching in International Business, International Business Negotiations, International Trade, International Management, International Marketing, E-Commerce (including Cross-Border E-Commerce), Global Supply Chain Management, International Finance, and related areas. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in international business and related discipline. Ability to teach online courses (asynchronous and synchronous) Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for overtime, nor benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials : To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Please note that applicants will be asked to provide original transcripts from their highest degree and two letters of reference upon hire. Please be advised that the University does check references as part of the employment process. Questions should be directed to Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41505&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Information Systems",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/26/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Information Systems FTE: Part-time, Less than 50% (0.50) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per 3-credit graduate course Position # 00695889 – Requisition #41505 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The Business School at the University of Colorado Denver (CU Denver) seeks to establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. Lecturer in Information Systems What you will do: Lecturers selected from this pool will teach Information Systems classes in the Business School at the University of Colorado Denver. Duties include preparing and delivering rigorous instruction aligned with curricular objectives and learning outcomes, supporting students from diverse backgrounds, assessing student learning, and adhering to program and university policies. Teaching may span areas such as AI and agentic systems, enterprise systems and platforms, cybersecurity, data and analytics, cloud and digital technologies, and other contemporary and emerging areas of Information Systems. Classes may be offered at the undergraduate or graduate level and delivered in person, online, or in hybrid formats. Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in Information Systems or closely related field. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least five years of duties and responsibilities. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Prior teaching experience in Information Systems or a closely related discipline. Teaching or professional expertise in one or more contemporary and emerging I.S areas, such as AI and agentic systems, enterprise systems and platforms, cybersecurity, data and analytics, cloud technologies, or other emerging technologies. Ability to connect technical concepts and emerging technologies with managerial, strategic, and organizational application. Experience incorporating current industry practices and applied learning into the classroom. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in Information Systems or a related discipline. Demonstrated commitment to effective teaching, mentoring, and student learning. Ability to translate disciplinary knowledge and industry practices into effective classroom learning. Commitment to inclusive and equitable teaching practices that support students from diverse backgrounds. Effective written and oral communication skills. Ability to plan, develop, and deliver courses aligned with established learning objectives and program expectations. Ability to work collaboratively and maintain effective relationships with faculty, staff, students, and other university stakeholders. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [ Oct 27, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: A cover letter which specifically addresses job requirements and outlines qualifications Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41504&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/25/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Full-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Entrepreneurship FTE : Part-Time, Less than 50% (0.50) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: Minimum $6,000+ depending on total course enrollment at census date Position # 00790682 – Requisition #41504 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Denver Business School seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. The Jake Jabs Center for Entrepreneurship at the CU Denver Business School seeks to establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers in Entrepreneurship and Innovation, from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. This posting does not necessarily reflect a current, open position. This temporary Lecturer pool is anticipated to remain continuously active through January 2027, at which point all applications will be cleared from the pool. Applicants will be welcome to apply to future pools after that date. Lecturer in Entrepreneurship What you will do: Lecturers selected from this pool will teach Entrepreneurship classes in the CU Denver Business School. Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Lecturers teaching these classes will instruct in either one or multiple teaching modalities (in-person, online-remote, or hybrid). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in a closely related field to the course topic. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least three years of duties and responsibilities. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Prior experience teaching in higher education. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in related discipline. Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of diversity, equity, and inclusion with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at a minimum of $6,000 per three-credit course; the rate may be increased depending on total course enrollment at census date. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Clair Seville, Jake Jabs Center for Entrepreneurship Assistant Director of Operations, at clair.seville@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41501&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Finance",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/25/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Finance FTE: Part Time, Less than 50% (0.50) FTE | In- Person Salary Range : $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per 3-credit graduate course Position # 00683765 – Requisition #41501 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Denver Business School seeks to establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers in Finance from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions for the 2026-2027 academic year will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. Lecturer in Finance What you will do: Lecturers selected from this pool will teach Finance classes in the CU Denver Business School. Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Lecturers teaching these classes will instruct in either one or multiple teaching modalities (in-person, online-remote, or hybrid). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in Finance or closely related field. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least two years of duties and responsibilities. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) PhD in Finance or closely related field. Prior online teaching experience in Finance and the record of teaching multiple finance courses. Professional designations such as CFA AND CFP are preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in related discipline. Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of diversity, equity, and inclusion with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026].. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Please note that upon hire, applicants will be asked to provide original transcript(s) of their highest degree and two (2) letters of recommendation. Questions should be directed to Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41500&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Business Analytics",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/25/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Business Analytics FTE: Part Time, Less than 50% (0.50) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range : $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per 3-credit graduate course Position # 00350293 – Requisition #41500 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Denver Business School is seeking applications for a Lecturer in Business Analytics position. This posting will establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions for the 2026-2027 academic year will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. Lecturer in Business Analytics What you will do: The Lecturer(s) selected will teach Business Analytics courses at the CU Denver Business School. Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Classes will be facilitated in varying modalities (in person, hybrid, or online). Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in Operations Research, Statistics, Computer Science, Applied Mathematics, Operations Management, or closely related field. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Prior experience teaching in Business Analytics, Statistics, Operations Management, or Operations Research, and the record of teaching multiple analytics-focused courses. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least three years of duties and responsibilities. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in related discipline. Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Please note that applicants will be asked to provide original transcripts from their highest degree and two letters of recommendation upon hire. Please be advised that the University does check references as part of the employment process. Questions should be directed to Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41499&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Accounting",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/25/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Accounting FTE: Full-time or part-time: Part- Time Salary Range: $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per 3-credit graduate course Position #00601531 – Requisition #41499 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu. About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The CU Denver Business School is seeking applications for a Lecturer in Accounting position. This posting will establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions for the 2025-2026 academic year will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. Lecturer in Accounting What you will do: The Lecturer(s) selected will teach in the Accounting discipline at the CU Denver Business School. Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Classes will be facilitated in varying modalities (in person, hybrid, remote or online). Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master's degree or terminal degree in Finance, Accounting, Payroll, Fiscal Reporting, Fiscal Management, Financial Forecasting, or a directly related field from an accredited institution and additional certifications, licensures, and/or trainings as applicable. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least five years of duties and responsibilities. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Prior experience teaching in Accounting. Professional certification/licensure in accounting or allied field, e.g., CPA. CMA, etc. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in related discipline. Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements The ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but may involve bending or reaching to retrieve items from shelves or drawers. This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). Please note that applicants will be asked to provide original transcripts from their highest degree and two letters of reference upon hire. Please be advised that the University does check references as part of the employment process. Questions should be directed to:Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
    },
    "https://cu.taleo.net/careersection/2/jobdetail.ftl?job=41496&lang=en": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Risk Management & Insurance",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/25/2027 Posted Date: Oct 27, 2026 Job category: Faculty Department: Business School Schedule: Part-time Position Details University of Colorado | Denver Faculty Level/Title: Lecturer Working Title: Lecturer in Risk Management & Insurance FTE: Part-Time Less than 50% (0.50) FTE | Hybrid Salary Range: $5,660.00 per 3-credit undergraduate course/$6,135.00 per combined undergrad/graduate courses. Position # 00708584 – Requisition #41496 Join the University of Colorado Denver About the University of Colorado Denver Millions of moments start at CU Denver, a place where innovation, research, and learning meet in the heart of a global city. We’re the state’s premier public urban research university with more than 100 in-demand, top-ranked bachelor’s, master’s, and doctoral degree programs. We partner with diverse learners—at any stage of their life and career—for transformative educational experiences. Across seven schools and colleges, our leading faculty inspires and works alongside students to solve complex challenges and produce impactful creative work. As part of the state’s largest university system, CU Denver is a major contributor to the Colorado economy, with 2,000 employees and an annual economic impact of $665 million. To learn more about how CU Denver helps learners meet their moment, visit ucdenver.edu . About the CU Denver Business School “Denver Built. Global Ready”. At the CU Denver Business School, we make the most of being deeply embedded in the heart of Denver and the nation’s fastest growing economy. You’ll find a welcoming, inclusive community that encourages what you bring with you and what you aspire to be. We’re ready to equip any future – locally and globally. We offer more choices than any other Business School in Colorado, with 14 Undergraduate Majors, 4 Industry Programs, 7 MBA Options, 3 Centers of Excellence, and 11 Master of Science Programs. We rank at the top for Social Mobility in Colorado, maintaining over three hundred Business relationships in Colorado and across the country. 80% of our career-minded students work while enrolled, opening doors and lowering barriers to success. CU Denver Business School is the #1 top-ranked national university in Colorado for campus ethnic diversity (US News). Job Description * Applications are accepted electronically ONLY at www.cu.edu/cu-careers * The University of Colorado Denver Business School seeks individuals with demonstrated commitment to creating an inclusive learning and working environment. We value the ability to engage effectively with students, faculty and staff of diverse backgrounds. The Business School at the University of Colorado Denver (CU Denver) seeks to establish and maintain a pool of Lecturers in Risk Management & Insurance from which future appointments to temporary, non-tenure-track positions will be made. Appointments will be part-time (less than 50% FTE) and will be made semester-by-semester, as teaching needs arise. This posting does not necessarily reflect a current, open position. This temporary Lecturer pool is anticipated to remain continuously active through January 2027, at which point all applications will be cleared from the pool. Applicants will be welcome to apply to future pools after that date. Lecturer in Risk Management & Insurance What you will do: Lecturers selected from this pool will teach Risk Management & Insurance classes in the Business School at the University of Colorado Denver. Duties include delivery of tailored instruction to a variety of language and cultural backgrounds in accordance with prescribed curricular objectives and outcomes, preparing for each class ahead of time with balanced rigorous lesson plans, assessing student progress according to curricular objectives and outcomes, and adhering to program policies and procedures by reporting student offenses (plagiarism, cheating, absences, etc.). Classes taught will be at either the undergraduate or graduate level and will generally be limited to three credit hours. Lecturers teaching these classes will instruct in either one or multiple teaching modalities (in-person, online-remote, or hybrid). Qualifications you already possess (Minimum Qualifications) Applicants must meet minimum qualifications at the time of hire. Master’s or higher degree in Business, Finance, Risk Management and Insurance, Marketing, or closely related field. Recent significant professional, technical, or managerial experience in the discipline related to the teaching assignment; at a minimum, significant experience is interpreted as at least 10 years of duties and responsibilities. Preferred Qualification to possess (Preferred Qualifications) Prior teaching experience in Risk Management and Insurance, in-person, online, and hybrid, or at least one of these modalities. Professional designations such as CPCU and ARM are a plus. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge and proficiency in related discipline. Demonstrated interest in mentoring and teaching in related discipline. Demonstrate an exceptional understanding of diversity, equity, and inclusion with a commitment to developing equitable practices. Ability to communicate effectively, both in writing and orally. Ability to demonstrate exceptional leadership qualities. Ability to effectively plan, establish and implement teaching goals and objectives independently without guidance and direction from other faculty. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees at all levels throughout the institution. Conditions of Employment Occasional work during the evening and/or weekends may be required. This position follows a hybrid work structure where employees can work remotely or from the office, as needed, based on demands of specific tasks or personal work preferences. Working from the office is encouraged when working on tasks that require a high degree of collaboration. Mental, Physical, and/or Environmental Requirements This position may be performed on site, and will require the ability to sit for extended periods, stand and walk occasionally, reach with hands and arms, use hands to manipulate a keyboard and mouse, and have good near vision for computer work; often requiring minimal lifting, but This position may be performed in a hybrid or remote environment, requiring the ability to work effectively in a remote setting. This includes maintaining a dedicated workspace free of excessive noise or distractions, reliable internet connectivity, and the ability to participate in virtual meetings for extended periods. Employees must be able to independently manage time, remain stationary for prolonged computer-based work, and transport necessary equipment (such as a laptop and peripherals) between their remote work location and the office as needed. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. The University will provide reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities throughout the employment application process. To request an accommodation pursuant to the Americans with Disabilities Act, please contact the Human Resources ADA Coordinator at workplaceengagement@ucdenver.edu . Employment Sponsorship Please be advised that this position is not eligible now or in the future for visa sponsorship. Compensation and Benefits The salary range (or hiring range) for this position has been established at $5,660.00 to $6135.00 depending upon course level. As a part-time teaching role, this position is not eligible for benefits. Information on University benefits programs, including eligibility, is located at Employee Services. The salary of the finalist(s) selected for this role will be set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to, internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. The above salary range (or hiring range) represents the University’s good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of possible compensation at the time of posting. This position is not eligible for overtime compensation. Application Deadline Applications for this pooled position will be accepted on a rolling basis for up to three (3) months from the posting date [Oct 27, 2026,]. Qualified applicants may be reviewed and approved for hire at any point during this period. Early application is encouraged, as the pool may close before the three‑month window if all openings are filled. Required Application Materials: To apply, please visit: http://www.cu.edu/cu-careers and attach: Curriculum vitae / Resume outlining experience(s). A cover letter which specifically addresses job requirements and outlines qualifications. List of three references (we will notify you prior to contacting both on and off-list references) Questions should be directed to Brandy Leggins-Baker; brandy.leggins-baker@ucdenver.edu . Background Check Policy The University of Colorado Denver strives to maintain a safe and productive educational, clinical, research and employment environment. All prospective employees and current employees must, therefore, consent to and pass background checks prior to any final appointment/employment."
